<main class="write-main pub-main google-workspace"><header class="writer-head"><div><span class="writer-kicker">Your selected calendars</span><h1>Private calendar refresh</h1><p>Keep a small private agenda current while email and publishing delivery remain independently controlled.</p></div><a class="wbtn" href="<?=url('/write/google#calendars')?>">Choose calendars</a></header>
<?php foreach(flashes()as$notice):?><p class="pub-card" role="status"><?=e($notice['message'])?></p><?php endforeach;?><?php if($error!==''):?><p class="pub-card" role="alert"><?=e($error)?></p><?php endif;?>
<section class="pub-card"><h2>Refresh preferences</h2><p>Only calendars you have selected are eligible. The encrypted cache covers yesterday and the next 30 days, storing event titles, times, locations and meeting links. Attendees, descriptions and attachments are excluded. Public booking availability always uses live provider checks.</p>
<form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="settings"><label class="pub-check"><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" value="1" <?=!empty($config['enabled'])?'checked':''?>> Refresh my selected calendars privately in the background</label><label class="pub-check"><input type="checkbox" name="push" value="1" <?=!empty($config['push'])?'checked':''?>> Also register Google change notifications for faster refresh</label><p>Notifications reveal no event content. Channels renew before expiry, and polling remains the fallback. Up to 30 selected calendars are supported; each worker invocation checks up to four due calendars. Turning refresh off removes the local cached event copies. Existing Google events stay intact.</p><button class="wbtn primary">Save refresh preferences</button></form></section>
<section class="pub-card"><div class="writer-head"><div><h2>Refresh status</h2><p><?=!empty($config['enabled'])?'Private background refresh is enabled. Failed reads retry with increasing delays, up to one hour. Check due calendars respects these delays.':'Private background refresh is off. You can still read the live agenda in Google workspace.'?></p></div><?php if(!empty($config['enabled'])):?><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><button class="wbtn" name="action" value="refresh">Check due calendars</button></form><?php endif;?></div>
<?php if(!$rows):?><p>Select calendars in Google workspace to get started.</p><?php endif;?>
<?php foreach($rows as$row):?><article class="pub-card"><h3><?=e($row['calendar'])?></h3><p><?=e($row['account'])?></p><dl><dt>Last complete refresh</dt><dd><?=$row['observed']?e(gmdate('j M Y H:i',$row['observed']).' UTC'):'Not recorded'?></dd><?php if(!empty($row['attempted'])):?><dt>Last attempt</dt><dd><?=e(gmdate('j M Y H:i',$row['attempted']).' UTC')?></dd><?php endif;?><?php if(!empty($row['retry_at'])):?><dt>Next retry eligible</dt><dd><?=e(gmdate('j M Y H:i',$row['retry_at']).' UTC')?></dd><?php endif;?><dt>Method</dt><dd><?=e($row['mode'])?></dd><dt>Events in this bounded snapshot</dt><dd><?=$row['observed']?(int)$row['count']:'Not available'?></dd><dt>Notification expiry</dt><dd><?=$row['expires']?e(gmdate('j M Y H:i',$row['expires']).' UTC'):'Polling only'?></dd></dl><?php if($row['error']||$row['push_error']):?><p role="status"><?=e(trim($row['error'].' '.$row['push_error']))?></p><p><a href="<?=url('/write/google#calendars')?>">Review the selected account and reconnect Google access</a>. Choose the same Google identity when asked; a new identity creates a separate connection and does not replace the failing one. No other calendar selection is changed automatically.</p><?php endif;?></article><?php endforeach;?></section></main>
